example.report:
VERDICT: Do not ship.
SCOPE: AddRow in ActivityTableWriter.cs, and its caller in ChartRefresh.cs.
COUNTS: 1 blocker, 1 high, 1 medium.

TOP RISK: A milestone row crashes the refresh, because Finish is read as if it must exist.

FINDINGS
| # | Severity | Where | Issue |
|---|----------|-------|-------|
| 1 | P0 | ActivityTableWriter.cs:42 | Crash when Finish is null. Milestones are legal rows. |
| 2 | P1 | ActivityTableWriter.cs:44 | Name is trimmed without a null check. |
| 3 | P2 | AddRow tests | No test feeds null Finish or blank Name. The rejection path is untested. |

DETAIL

### 1. Crash when Finish is null (P0)
Where: ActivityTableWriter.cs:42
What happens: the code calls Value on Finish. A milestone row has no Finish.
Why it matters: one legal row stops the whole refresh. The user sees a generic error.
Proof: the schema note says Finish is optional. The caller passes the row unchanged. Guess on the exact message; the throw is certain.
Fix: read Start as required. Read Finish only when it exists.
Behaviour change: none. Rows with a Finish behave as before.

public void AddRow(ActivityRow row)
{
    var start = row.Start
        ?? throw new ArgumentException("Start is required.", nameof(row));

    var finish = row.Finish ?? start;
    if (finish < start) finish = start;

    var name = row.Name?.Trim() ?? string.Empty;
    table.Rows.Add(start, finish, name);
}

### 2. Name is trimmed without a null check (P1)
Where: ActivityTableWriter.cs:44
What happens: a null Name throws before the row is added.
Why it matters: the failure is invisible. The row is lost, and the log says nothing useful.
Fix: fall back to an empty string, as shown above. Add a test for the blank case.

### 3. The rejection path is untested (P2)
Where: the AddRow tests
What happens: only a complete row is tested.
Why it matters: the crash above was reachable, and no test noticed.
Fix: add two tests.

[Fact]
public void AddRow_UsesStart_WhenFinishIsNull()
{
    var row = new ActivityRow { Start = new DateOnly(2026, 1, 1), Finish = null, Name = "Kickoff" };
    table.AddRow(row);
    Assert.Equal(new DateOnly(2026, 1, 1), table.Rows[0].Finish);
}

[Fact]
public void AddRow_AcceptsNullName()
{
    var row = new ActivityRow { Start = new DateOnly(2026, 1, 1), Finish = null, Name = null };
    var error = Record.Exception(() => table.AddRow(row));
    Assert.Null(error);
}

QUESTIONS
- Should a null Name be rejected instead of replaced with an empty string? The schema note does not say.

NEXT: code mode applies findings 1 to 3. Re-review after the tests exist.
